---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/breadcrumbs.astro'
import Link from '@/components/link.astro'
import PageHead from '@/components/page-head.astro'
import Layout from '@/layouts/layout.astro'
---

<Layout class="max-w-4xl">
  <PageHead slot="head" title="About" />
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About', icon: 'lucide:info' }]} />

  <div class="bg-muted/30 rounded-lg border font-mono text-sm">
    <div class="border-b px-4 py-3">
      <span class="text-primary">───[nightxade@nightsite ~]</span><span class="text-muted-foreground">$ whoami</span>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 px-4 py-4">

      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      hey! I'm <span class="text-primary font-semibold">nightxade</span>, known irl as Matthew Cai. I'm currently attending the <span class="font-medium" style="color: #fdb515">University of California, Berkeley</span><img src="/logos/ucb.svg" class="inline ml-1.5 size-4 align-middle" alt="" />, majoring in <span style="color: #7df9ff">Electrical Engineering and Computer Sciences</span>. As of May 2026, I have just completed my second year of school; I plan to graduate after 2 more semesters of school (out-of-state tuition is expensive :&lt;).
      </p>

      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      I'm interested in quite a few different areas of computer science, here's my current shortlist: security, microarchitecture, ML systems, AI safety, reinforcement learning, and distributed systems. Thus, I'm trying to cram as many classes as I possibly can into my 6 college semesters, and read my way through all the subjects I'm passionate about. I started reading so much that I began <Link href="/reading" class="text-foreground" underline>tracking my reading</Link> too, as a way of recording my progress and learning journey. If you have any reading or subject recommendations, please send them my way! I'm also a devout believer in <span style="color: #d34516">Rust</span><img src="/logos/rust-white.png" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" /> (cult member?), though my favorite languages additionally extend to <span style="color: #ffffff">C/C++</span><img src="/logos/c++.svg" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" /> and (somewhat reluctantly, in spite of its type system) <span style="color: #4b8bbe">Python</span><img src="/logos/python.svg" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" /> too. I want to eventually be a programming language polyglot; at the moment, I'd like to learn more functional programming and hardware description languages.
      </p>

      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      I'm a semi-active cybersecurity capture the flag (CTF) player — I main crypto/pwn on <Link href="https://spl.team/" class="text-foreground" underline>Squid Proxy Lovers</Link><img src="/logos/spl.svg" class="inline ml-1.5 size-4 align-middle" alt="" /> and <span class="text-foreground">Cosmic Bit Flip</span><img src="/logos/cbf.png" class="inline ml-1.5 size-4 align-middle" alt="" />. I've realized recently that I enjoy reading vulnerability research blogs and papers even more :skull:. I used to author <Link href="/writeups" class="text-foreground" underline>writeups</Link> for all the challenges I solved; perhaps I'll pick it up again in the future, provided LLMs haven't killed off CTFs by that point... :(
      </p>

      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      I used to be math competition kid, primarily in middle school. (For a while, my proudest achievement was qualifying for the AIME in 8th grade)! I've since stepped away from the scene, but I still retain an interest in mathematics — during my freshman year of college, I studied abstract algebra and Galois theory. Perhaps I'll take the Putnam for fun at some point! I also really enjoy playing the <span class="line-through">24</span> 1000 game from time to time :D
      </p>

      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      Outside of computer science, I'm broadly interested in quantum computing, most science subjects (bio, chem, astronomy, physics), and world history. In my limited free time, I watch F1<img src="/logos/f1.png" class="inline ml-1 h-2 w-auto align-middle" alt="" /> and MotoGP<img src="/logos/motogp.png" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle invert" alt="" />, read manhua, grind monkeytype<img src="/logos/monkeytype.png" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" /> and bullet chess, and follow CounterStrike<img src="/logos/cs2.png" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" /> esports. I'm a former Valorant<img src="/logos/valorant.png" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" /> addict, and previously played Geometry Dash<img src="/logos/gd.svg" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" />, Brawl Stars<img src="/logos/brawlstars.png" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" />, Clash Royale<img src="/logos/clashroyale.jpg" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" />, Terraria<img src="/logos/terraria.png" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle object-cover" alt="" />, and Minecraft<img src="/logos/minecraft.png" class="inline ml-1 size-4 align-middle" alt="" />. I also really <em>really</em> like <span class="font-bold">cats</span>! :3
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
